{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2930.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-11 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Political Economy of Public Policy Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting February 01, 2027, and ending after 6 years Postdoctoral Researcher in Quantitative Social Science Methodology with a strong focus on Political Economy or Comparative Public Policy The Department of Socioeconomics at WU Vienna University of Economics and Business invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track postdoctoral position. We seek a researcher who combines an equally ambitious research agenda in political economy or comparative public policy and in modern quantitative research designs. The position offers the opportunity to pursue theoretically informed, empirically rigorous research in an active and internationally oriented social science environment. We welcome applicants who ask consequential questions about politics, institutions, and socioeconomic change—and bring compelling research designs to bear on them. Substantive interests are open within political economy and comparative public policy. Your research and contribution You will develop an independent research agenda, produce work aimed at leading international journals, and contribute actively to the department’s intellectual life through research exchange and collaboration. We are particularly interested in candidates whose work demonstrates a thoughtful connection between substantive questions, theoretical arguments, and empirical identification. Relevant approaches include experimental and quasi-experimental designs, survey experiments, and advanced observational methods. We value careful measurement, transparent and reproducible research practices, and sound judgment about what the evidence can and cannot establish. Teaching in social science methodology is a central part of the position. You will contribute to the department’s quantitative methods teaching, helping students develop the skills to formulate research questions, assess research designs, and conduct rigorous empirical analyses. There may also be opportunities to teach substantive courses in your area of expertise. Teaching is predominantly in English. An interest in developing externally funded research projects and strengthening international research connections is welcome. Knowledge of German is an asset. How to apply Please apply through WU’s online recruitment system, using position ID 2930. Your application should include: A cover letter outlining your research agenda, methodological expertise, and fit with the position. A curriculum vitae, including your publications. A list of courses taught. Please complete the WU application form. Do not include research papers or references at this stage. We look forward to learning about your research and the contribution you would make to our department. What to expect Conducting independent research: You will actively contribute to the research at the Department of Socioeconomics, publish in top journals in the field, and present at international academic conferences. Teaching and supporting courses: You will plan and teach courses (4 semester hours per week/2 courses each semester) in the Bachelor and Master programs of the Department of Socioeconomics. Supervising students: You will be available to answer students’ questions and act as a supervisor for bachelor’s and master’s theses. Benefiting from a strong researcher environment: You will work in an excellent, internationally connected team that supports you in developing your own research projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. Organizational tasks: As part of the team, you will support selected organizational tasks of the department and/or the institute. Building up a professional network: You will be using the post-doc phase to establish yourself as an independent researcher and expand your own professional network, keeping the WU’s third mission and societal engagement in mind. What you have to offer Your profile We are looking for applicants with: Academic degree: A PhD or equivalent qualification in political science or a closely related discipline. Research Profile: A distinctive research agenda in political economy or comparative public policy, with the potential to make significant contributions to international scholarship. Methodological Expertise: A research agenda in quantitative social science methodology. Research Excellence: Evidence of research excellence appropriate to career stage, demonstrated through publications and a pipeline of research aimed at leading social science journals. Teaching experience: Expertise in advanced quantitative methods and an experience in teaching research methods. Teaching Excellence: A commitment to excellent teaching and the ability to explain demanding methodological concepts clearly, ideally supported by experience teaching quantitative social science methods. Teamwork: A collaborative approach and a willingness to participate actively in the department’s research and teaching community. What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,079.50 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2930). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Universitaetsassistentin-post-doc-Non-Tenure-Track-de-j2933.html": {
      "title": "Universitätsassistent*in post doc Non Tenure Track",
      "description": "Stellenangebot Universitätsassistent*in post doc Non Tenure Track bei think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. DEUTSCH ENGLISH Jobangebote Karriere @ WU Wien Zurück Jetzt bewerben! Universitätsassistent*in post doc Non Tenure Track Wirtschaftsuniversität Wien Forschung, Entwicklung, Lehre Vollzeit Publizierung bis: 04.11.2026 Sie möchten Zusammenhänge verstehen und Grundlegendes bewegen? Bei uns finden Sie das Umfeld, in dem Sie Ihr Potenzial entfalten können. An einer der größten und modernsten Wirtschaftsuniversitäten Europas. Auf einem Campus, an dem Arbeitsqualität auch Lebensqualität ist. Wir suchen Verstärkung in der Abteilung für Kartellrecht Vollzeit, 40 Stunden/Woche Ab 15.11.2026 befristet für die Dauer von 4 Jahre Wir laden besonders Personen mit Behinderung ein, sich bei entsprechender Qualifikation zu bewerben. Bei Bedarf ist ein geringeres Beschäftigungsausmaß möglich. Am Institut für Unternehmensrecht, Abteilung für Kartellrecht (Univ.-Prof. Dr. Georg Eckert) wird eine Stelle als Universitätsassistent*in post doc besetzt. Die Stelle ist darauf ausgerichtet, dass Sie Ihre Habilitation im Fach Unternehmensrecht innerhalb der Vertragslaufzeit abschließen. Sie arbeiten in einem kooperativen Team, in dem interdisziplinäre Perspektiven - etwa an der Schnittstelle von Recht und Ökonomie – ausdrücklich willkommen sind. Was Sie erwartet Habilitation: Sie verfolgen ein eigenständiges Habilitationsprojekt im Unternehmensrecht mit dem Ziel, die Lehrbefugnis innerhalb der Vertragslaufzeit zu erlangen, und werden dabei aktiv begleitet. Forschung: Sie forschen und publizieren im Kartellrecht, im Gesellschafts- und Rechnungslegungsrecht und in weiteren Teilgebieten des Unternehmensrechts in nationalen und internationalen Fachzeitschriften. Publikationsprojekte: Sie wirken an Kommentar- und Handbuchprojekten sowie an international besetzten, rechtsvergleichenden Herausgeberprojekten mit. Lehre: Sie halten selbständig Lehrveranstaltungen im Unternehmensrecht, insbesondere in den unternehmensrechtlichen Pflichtfächern, im Kartellrecht und im Recht der Rechnungslegung im kollektivvertraglich vorgesehenen Ausmaß ab, prüfen und betreuen Bachelor- und Masterarbeiten. Internationalisierung: Sie präsentieren Ihre Forschung auf Tagungen im In- und Ausland und bauen internationale Kontakte auf, etwa durch Forschungsaufenthalte. Drittmittel: Sie entwickeln Anträge auf Forschungsförderung bzw. wirken daran mit. Organisation: Sie übernehmen Organisations-, Verwaltungs- und Evaluierungsaufgaben und bringen sich in die universitäre Selbstverwaltung ein Was Sie mitbringen Doktorat: abgeschlossenes Doktoratsstudium der Rechtswissenschaften (oder gleichwertiger in- oder ausländischer Abschluss) mit Schwerpunkt im Unternehmensrecht. Publikationen: einschlägige wissenschaftliche Veröffentlichungen im Kartellrecht sowie in mindestens einem weiteren Teilgebiet des Unternehmensrechts (etwa Gesellschafts-, Kapitalmarkt- oder Rechnungslegungsrecht). Lehre: mehrjährige Erfahrung in selbständiger universitärer Lehre im Unternehmens- oder Kartellrecht einschließlich Prüfungstätigkeit. Habilitationsvorhaben: ein Habilitationsvorhaben im Unternehmensrecht, das innerhalb von vier Jahren abgeschlossen werden kann. Sprache: ausgezeichnete Deutschkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift (Lehre in deutscher Sprache) und gute Englischkenntnisse. Multimedia Lehr-Bereitschaft: Sie sind bereit, multimediale Lehr- und Lernformate anzuwenden Dissertation auf dem Gebiet des Kartellrechts erwünscht, idealerweise mit Auszeichnung abgeschlossen und in einer einschlägigen wissenschaftlichen Schriftenreihe eines international tätigen Fachverlags veröffentlicht Idealerweise Beiträge in internationalen Fachzeitschriften und in der Kommentar- und Handbuchliteratur sowie Mitwirkung an international besetzten, rechtsvergleichenden Herausgeberprojekten; veröffentlichte oder abgabefertige Vorarbeiten zum Habilitationsprojekt nachgewiesene didaktische Qualität (etwa Lehrveranstaltungsevaluierungen, Lehrpreise oder -nominierungen), Erfahrung in der Betreuung wissenschaftlicher Arbeiten erwünscht Erfahrung in der Einwerbung von Fördermitteln sowie in Organisation und universitärer Selbstverwaltung von Vorteil internationale Erfahrung, etwa Forschungsaufenthalte an ausländischen Universitäten, Vortragstätigkeit im Ausland, Einbindung in internationale Nachwuchsnetzwerke erwünscht Was wir Ihnen bieten Flexible Arbeitszeiten Vielfältiges Angebot an Weiterbildung Zahlreiche Benefits , von Betriebsarzt über Sportangebote und Essenszuschuss bis hin zu vielfältigen Mitarbeitenden-Rabatten Sinnstiftende Arbeit , in einem weltoffenen, inklusiven und familienfreundlichen Arbeitsklima Architektonisch herausragender, moderner Campus mitten in Wien Inspirierendes Campusleben mit über 2.400 Mitarbeitenden in Forschung, Lehre und Verwaltung und rund 21.500 Studierenden Sehr gute öffentliche Erreichbarkeit Neugierig geworden? Mehr darüber was die WU als Arbeitgeberin besonders macht, erfahren Sie unter www.wu.ac.at/benefits Das monatliche Mindestentgelt beträgt 5.014,30 Euro brutto. Gleichwertige Vordienstzeiten können zu einem höheren Einstiegsgehalt führen. Darüber hinaus bieten wir eine Vielzahl an attraktiven Sozialleistungen an. Wollen Sie Teil der WU werden? Dann bewerben Sie sich bitte bis spätestens 04.11.2026 (Kennzahl: 2933). Wir freuen uns auf Sie! Bewerbungsunterlagen Motivationsschreiben wissenschaftlicher Lebenslauf mit Publikations- und Lehrverzeichnis (inkl. Lehrevaluierungen, soweit vorhanden) Skizze des Habilitationsprojekts mit Arbeits- und Zeitplan (max. 3 Seiten) Nachweis des abgeschlossenen Doktorats bis zu drei Schriftproben (optional) Kontaktdaten von zwei Referenzpersonen Fragen beantwortet Univ.-Prof. Dr. Georg Eckert (eckert.georg@wu.ac.at). Die WU schätzt Diversität und Inklusion und bemüht sich aktiv um ein vielfältiges wissenschaftliches Team. Wir laden insbesondere Frauen herzlich zur Bewerbung ein. Sie sind sich nicht sicher, ob Ihr Profil unseren Anforderungen entspricht? Bewerben Sie sich trotzdem! Frauen werden bei gleicher Qualifikation bevorzugt aufgenommen. Bewerber*innen mit Behinderungen werden in allen Phasen des Bewerbungsprozesses unterstützt. Die Qualifikationen der Bewerber*innen werden im Kontext des jeweiligen akademischen Werdegangs bewertet. IMPRESSUM DATENSCHUTZ Einstellungen Cookies Notwendige Cookies Diese Cookies sind für die Funktionalität unserer Website erforderlich\nund können in unserem System nicht ausgeschaltet werden. Vorausgewählt Webstatistik Wir verwenden diese Cookies, um statistische Informationen über unsere Website\nbereitzustellen. Sie werden zur Leistungsmessung und -verbesserung verwendet. Wählen Soziale Netzwerke & Embeds Auf einigen Seiten betten wir Inhalte von Sozialen Netzwerken und anderen Diensten ein. Dadurch können Ihre personenbezogenen Daten an den Betreiber des Portals, von dem der Inhalt stammt, weitergegeben werden, so dass dieser Ihr Verhalten analysieren kann. Wählen Notwendige Cookies Webstatistik"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2936.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-11 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Department of Business Analytics and Decision Sciences Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting January 01, 2027, and ending after 3 years Do you want to shape the interface of behavioral science and AI, using language models as research tools and models of the mind, and using behavioral science to evaluate and improve AI? Join a newly established department as a fixed-term Assistant Professor and help build its research program from day one. What to expect Conduct cutting-edge research: You will work at the intersection of behavioral science and AI, in either direction: using large language models as tools, measurement instruments, and simulations of human cognition and behavior (e.g., silicon sampling) for the behavioral sciences, or using behavioral science theory and methods to characterize, evaluate, and improve AI systems, for example by studying their reasoning, biases, and decision making, their psychological profiles, their behavior in interaction with humans, or questions of AI safety. You will publish your findings in leading interdisciplinary journals and conference proceedings Develop methods and tools: You will develop open-source methods, datasets, and software that make state-of-the-art AI accessible to behavioral researchers, or that bring behavioral science methods to the evaluation and improvement of AI systems, such as behavioral benchmarks and experimental paradigms for testing AI Pursue your own agenda: You will have substantial freedom and resources to advance your own research program and establish yourself as an independent scientist Teach in an international program: You will plan and teach courses in English at the intersection of AI, data science, and behavioral science, and co-supervise bachelor's and master's theses Collaborate internationally: You will work within an active international network spanning cognitive science, AI, and decision science Grow your scientific profile: You will use this fixed-term assistant professorship to expand your networks, gain experience in grant acquisition, and prepare the next step of your academic career What you have to offer Academic degree: You have completed (or are about to complete) a doctoral degree in psychology, cognitive science, economics, computer science, or a related field with excellent results Research focus: Your research, as documented by your publications and research statement, connects large language models and the behavioral sciences, for example by using them as methodological tools, measurement instruments, or simulations of human cognition and behavior, or by applying behavioral science methods to characterize, evaluate, or improve the behavior of AI systems, for example their reasoning and decision making, psychological profiles and behavioral robustness, interactions with humans, or safety Publication record: You have an excellent publication record for your career stage, including first-authored publications in leading international peer-reviewed journals or top-tier conference proceedings relevant to the field Technical expertise: You have strong programming skills (Python or R) and substantial hands-on experience with large language models, including open-source models experience Open science: Experience with open and reproducible research practices (e.g., preregistration, open data and code, open-source software) is a strong asset Conceptual depth: You are interested in the theoretical and conceptual foundations of human and machine behavior and can connect empirical work to broader questions in behavioral science and AI Teaching readiness: You have experience creating accessible scientific materials (e.g., tutorials, workshops) and are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats Language skills: You have excellent English skills; German skills are not mandatory but an advantage Engagement: You work independently, take initiative, and enjoy collaborative work in an interdisciplinary team What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,079.50 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2936). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2943.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-25 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Department of Business Communication Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting March 01, 2027, and ending after 6 years Strategic communication as the communication that is substantial for the survival and sustained success of social entities is an indispensable organizational function in the 21st century. The study of strategic communication is a key field of research and teaching at the Department of Business Communication. We are therefore looking for excellent applicants with a focus on research and teaching in the field of strategic communication (e.g., advertising, marketing communication, corporate communication, public relations or political communication). Are you interested? Then apply and become a member of our creative, international, and inspiring team at the Department of Business Communication at WU Vienna. What to expect Development of research and professional network: Develop and maintain a network with the world’s leading researchers in strategic communication and build a professional network of professional communicators in Vienna and beyond. Independent research work: You will be independently gathering data, working with cooperation partners and companies to conduct research with practical relevance, and publishing your findings in top journals as well as presenting them at conferences. Teaching: You will be planning and teaching courses (4 hrs. per week / 2 courses each semester), with a focus on business communication. Student support: You will be available to answer students’ questions and act as an advisor for bachelor’s and master’s theses. Organizational and administrative support: You will be organizing and evaluating teaching activities and supporting the master’s program. Learning from top researchers: You will be working together with renowned researchers in your field and learning from them. Teamwork: You’ll be working to advance research in your field, which also includes (collaborative) funding applications and acquisition of third-party funds. What you have to offer Doctoral Degree / PhD in communication studies or a related field (e.g., economics, sociology, linguistics, psychology, data science, political science). Subject-specific competences in the fields of strategic communication (e.g., advertising, marketing communication, corporate communication, public relations or political communication). Methodological knowledge: in-depth knowledge and proven experience of data analysis and quantitative social science research methods; knowledge of and experience in computational social science or NLP. Research funding: commitment to and potential experience in attracting research funding. Teaching experience: Experience in teaching classes and supervising BA and MA theses is advantageous. Language skills: fluent command of English at C1 level, and willingness to learn German (if not already a proficient German speaker). IT Skills: Expert knowledge of R or Python is required; further programming skills are desirable. Publications and outreach: experience in publishing and presenting research internationally. International academic experience demonstrated by presentations at international conferences, longer stays abroad, or international work experience outside of Austria, is expected. Research program: interest in developing your own research focus and pursuing your habilitation project. Do you want to join the team at the Department of Business Communication? Then please submit your application in English including: Curriculum vitae Motivation letter One academic publication as an example of your work Please direct any questions to Prof. Dr. Marc Jungblut E-Mail: marc.jungblut@wu.ac.at Web: https://www.wu.ac.at/bizcomm/sok What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,079.50 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 25, 2026 (ID 2943). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2947.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-18 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Cognition & Behavior Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting as soon as possible, and limited until December 31, 2027 The position is part of the Institute for Cognition and Behavior headed by Prof. Susann Fiedler. We investigate how attention, motivation and social contexts shape judgment and behavior. Current research includes belief formation and updating, motivated cognition and willful ignorance, cooperation and ethical decisions, and the effects of AI on human judgment, learning and scientific work. We combine laboratory and online experiments with process tracing. Applicants should connect with at least one of these areas; expertise across all topics is not required. What to expect Independently design and conduct laboratory and online experiments, including work on ongoing projects, using the institute’s participant pool and experimental and eye-tracking facilities. Take responsibility for defined research projects, coordinate study implementation and research assistants, and contribute methodological expertise and constructive feedback to the team. Contribute to teaching and student supervision in business psychology and decision sciences, including the specialization “Decision Sciences” Attendance of international conferences Publication of research projects in international journals What you have to offer Completed (or close to finished) PhD in psychology, cognitive science, economics, business and management, or a closely related field. A research profile relevant to at least one of the institute’s areas, demonstrated through empirical research and manuscripts or publications. We assess the quality of the work and your own contribution relative to career stage. Strong skills in experimental design and quantitative analysis. Ability to analyze data independently using R, Python or comparable script-based statistical software. Excellent English and the ability to communicate research clearly in writing, teaching and scientific discussion. Collaborative working practices, and the ability to support junior researchers through constructive methodological feedback. Experience with eye-tracking, mouse-tracking or related process-tracing methods; online experiment programming; computational models of decision processes; or LLMs. Strength in one or more of these areas is welcome; expertise in all of them is not expected. Fluency in English required You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats Application documents and selection Please submit a CV, your publication/manuscript list, and one research paper or unpublished manuscript that best demonstrates your contribution. Instead of a conventional motivation letter, answer the following three questions (maximum 600 words in total; bullet points are welcome). 1. Using the submitted paper, describe a consequential methodological decision. What alternative did you consider, why did you choose your approach, and what limitation remained? 2. Choose one main finding from the paper. What other explanation could account for this finding? Describe a specific analysis or study that would help distinguish between the two explanations, and explain what results would support each. 3. State briefly how your research experience or future research plans connects with the institute’s research areas. A full project proposal is not required. Shortlisted applicants will be invited to interviews during the first two weeks of December. Language-editing tools may be used when preparing the application; if generative AI contributed to the substantive content, briefly state how and what you checked; this statement does not count towards the word limit. What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5.014,30 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 18, 2026 (ID 2947). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-in-Management-and-Org-eng-j2913.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track (in Management and Organisational Behaviour)",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track (in Management and Organisational Behaviour) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track (in Management and Organisational Behaviour) Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-18 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting December 01, 2026, and ending after 3 years The Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour, as part of the Department of Management, is dedicated to studying human behaviour in organisations. We particularly focus on research questions that relate to promoting positive behaviour in organisations and that enable individuals to reach their full potential and experience greater well-being at work. We also consider the contextual embeddedness of human behaviour at work, by studying the impact of emerging societal and technical developments and grand challenges, such as AI, changing workplace practices and preferences (e.g., WFH), political/economic uncertainty, and sustainability, on (positive) human behaviour in organisations. If these topics excite you, we look forward to receiving your application for the advertised position. What to expect Conduct research: You will actively contribute to the institute’s research projects on organisational behaviour and further develop your own ideas. Teach and support courses: You will teach and support courses in OB, for example in the existing SBWL programme of the institute (on the BSc level) as well as in the Department of Management’s Master programme. Supervise master’s and bachelor’s theses: You co-supervise master’s and independently supervise bachelor’s theses. Support organisation and administration: You will help fulfill the institute’s administrative responsibilities. Work as part of a team: You will join a team of committed researchers who collaboratively advance research projects. Benefit from a strong research environment: You will work in an excellent, internationally connected team that supports you in developing your own projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. What you have to offer Doctoral degree: You have successfully completed your doctoral degree in Business Administration, Management, or a related subject area, with a focus on Organisational Behaviour, or Work & Organisational Psychology, and demonstrate a strong commitment to research through promising publication projects. Peer-reviewed presentations at academic conferences and initial publications in journals listed on the WU Star Journal List or the Department of Management Journal List are an advantage. Passion for research: You are highly motivated to pursue an academic career and aim to publish your work in reputable scholarly journals. Relevant expertise and experience: You bring knowledge in areas that meaningfully connect with the focus of the Institute, such as investigating positive behaviours at work (e.g., motivation, proactivity/job crafting), or affect/well-being/meaningfulness in organisations. Ideally, you also have experience in studying human behaviour ‘in context’. Research methodology: You have in-depth training in quantitative methods including experience with common software tools (e.g., Mplus, R, Stata, SPSS) and/or qualitative research methods (e.g., grounded theory, thematic analysis). You have a clear understanding of the strengths and limitations of different methodological approaches. Ideally, you have some experience in using multi-method approaches in field research. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Teaching in German: You are also able and willing to teach courses in German. International experience and language skills: You can demonstrate international exposure in your studies. Strong English skills (both verbal and written) are mandatory. Digital skills: You are confident using standard software applications (e.g., Microsoft Office, video conferencing tools) and can quickly learn new systems. Engagement: You work independently, are organised, take initiative, and are excited to contribute as a team player. Required submission materials (as one PDF file, in this order): Cover letter, including your earliest possible and preferred start dates CV Personal statement (briefly outlining research, teaching, and service activities; max 3 pages) Contact information for 2–3 academic references (name, affiliation, e-mail) Copies of 1–2 research papers If available: teaching evaluations Transcripts of grade reports Additionally (as a separate PDF file): Full PhD thesis We are looking forward to hearing from you! If you have any questions regarding the position or application documents, don’t hesitate to contact Prof. Dr. Uta Bindl at uta.bindl@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,014.30 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 18, 2026 (ID 2913). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-tenure-track-qualification-agreement-eng-j2934.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, tenure track (qualification agreement)",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, tenure track (qualification agreement) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, tenure track (qualification agreement) Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-22 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Economic and Social History Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting October 01, 2027, and limited for 6 years A qualification agreement will be concluded at the start of the employment (§ 27 of the Collective Bargaining Agreement). Pursuant to WU’s Personnel Development Plan, this position can only be fixed-term for up to six years. Once all objectives agreed upon in the qualification agreement have been fulfilled, the employment relationship can be made permanent. Employees who have successfully completed a qualification agreement are classified as associate professors. From an organizational regulation perspective they belong to the group of professors. Three years after successful completion of the qualification agreement, they are entitled to apply for promotion to full professor according to the By-Laws of WU § 43a. We are inviting applications for an Assistant Professor position (tenure track) in the field of Economic History to join our institute. This tenure track assistant professor position offers the opportunity to advance an independent research profile, publish internationally, acquire funding and gain substantial teaching experience while working collaboratively within a close-knit group of colleagues who share a strong interest in the field. Join an ambitious, internationally connected academic environment to take the next step in your academic career. What to expect Development of an internationally oriented research profile Publications in relevant high-quality outlets and presentations at relevant international conferences Teaching at BSc and MSc level (usually 4h/week per semester, 8h/week after tenure), collaboration in the development of the institute’s teaching portfolio Collaboration and independent supervision of BSc and MSc theses Participation in teaching and research administration within the academic self-administration at WU Independent or collaborative preparation of applications for third-party funded research projects. What you have to offer PhD/doctorate in Economic and/or Social Sciences (including Economic History). Proven research focus on topics relating to Economic History; applications from all areas of quantitative economic history are welcome. Excellent command of quantitative empirical methods of the economic and social sciences; the use of modern use of modern econometric and/or data science methods is expected Ability to develop and work with relevant datasets for the aforementioned research focus Publication(s) and/or forthcoming articles in leading journals and/or monograph(s) with academic publishers. Demonstrated active engagement with the international academic community, for example, through collaboration with international coauthors, research visits at other universities, or presentations at leading academic conferences. Candidates must have completed their PhD at a university other than WU or have at least two years of postdoctoral working experience at another university. It is an advantage if they demonstrate international academic experience—such as a PhD from a non-Austrian university or postdoctoral work at a non-Austrian academic institution for at least two years. Excellent spoken and written English skills ; German skills are not required, but knowledge and/or willingness to acquire them will be an advantage, as they improve flexibility in teaching. Experience in university teaching , preferably in the announced area of expertise, ability to teach in English and commitment to excellence in teaching Experience in applying for competitive research grants is not strictly required, but will be of advantage Willingness to engage in interdisciplinary research and teaching collaborations within the Department of Socioeconomics and at WU. Required submission materials: C.V. including list of publications Cover letter Writing sample, e.g., job market paper Research statement Teaching statement Two letters of reference Additional publications/manuscripts (optional) What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Living and working in one of the world’s most livable cities . Tax incentive for eligible international researchers moving to Austria. Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,980.80 (14 times per year). In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 22, 2026 (ID 2934). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-tenure-track-qualification-agreement-eng-j2907.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-11 WU Vienna University of Economics and Business combines excellence with responsibility. Its rare triple accreditation by EQUIS, AACSB, and AMBA is a guarantee for the highest quality research and teaching in the fields of business, economics, and business law. WU’s research is characterized by a wide diversity of disciplines practiced at WU, allowing researchers to deal with even the most complex research questions. International cooperation is very important to WU, and we encourage and support both faculty and student mobility. WU is also very aware of its responsibility to its students, faculty, and staff and is committed to gender equality, equal opportunities, accessibility, family-friendly working conditions, and sustainability. The Institute for Accounting and Auditing is looking for an Assistant Professor in Accounting Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting July 01, 2027, or soon thereafter, and limited for 6 years A qualification agreement will be concluded at the start of the employment (§ 27 of the Collective Bargaining Agreement). Pursuant to WU’s Personnel Development Plan, this position can only be fixed-term for up to six years. Once all objectives agreed upon in the qualification agreement have been fulfilled, the employment relationship can be made permanent. Employees who have successfully completed a qualification agreement are classified as associate professors. From an organizational regulation perspective they belong to the group of professors. Three years after successful completion of the qualification agreement, they are entitled to apply for promotion to full professor according to the By-Laws of WU § 43a. We are inviting applications for an Assistant Professor position (tenure track) in the field of financial accounting to join our institute. Members of the recruiting committee will attend the 2026 EAA Talent Workshop in Madrid and conduct interviews with prospective candidates. Candidates interested in this position are encouraged to attend the workshop and meet with us there. What to expect International faculty with a publication record in top tier accounting journals (e.g., The Accounting Review, Journal of Accounting Research, Journal of Accounting and Economics, Review of Accounting Studies). Strong international research network with regular guests from top-tier universities at our conferences and research seminars. Competitive compensation and strong research support, including research funding, data availability, and attractive teaching conditions. Tax incentive for eligible international researchers moving to Austria. Strong ties to business practice, professional associations, and policymakers. Highly motivated students with accounting majors in undergraduate, graduate, and PhD programs. What you have to offer We invite applications from researchers in the field of financial accounting. High-quality research using quantitative methods, with strong potential to publish in top-tier accounting journals. A completed PhD degree or anticipation to complete a PhD degree in the current academic year. Demonstrated active engagement with the international academic community, for example, through collaboration with international coauthors, research visits at other universities, or presentations at leading academic conferences. Candidates must have completed their PhD at a university other than WU or have at least two years of postdoctoral working experience at another university. It is an advantage if they demonstrate international academic experience—such as a PhD from a non-Austrian university or postdoctoral work at a non-Austrian academic institution for at least two years. The ability to teach in English and commitment to excellence in teaching. Required submission materials: C.V. Cover letter Job market paper Research statement Teaching statement Three letters of reference Additional papers (optional) For further information about the position, please contact Professor Zoltán Novotny-Farkas, at zoltan.novotny-farkas@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,980.80 (14 times per year). In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2907). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"
