      "title": "Stellenangebot Office Koordinator*in bei think:impact",
      "description": "Stellenangebot Office Koordinator*in bei think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. Um Ihnen einen bestmöglichen Service zu bieten und die Verwendung mancher Funktionen zu erleichtern, verwenden wir Cookies. Mit der Nutzung dieser Seite erklären Sie sich mit der Verwendung von Cookies einverstanden. Die Einwilligung kann jeder Zeit mit Wirkung für die Zukunft widerrufen werden. Mehr Informationen darüber, welche Daten gespeichert werden, erhalten Sie hier. . Ja, ich bin einverstanden Cookies anpassen Ablehnen DEUTSCH ENGLISH Jobangebote Karriere @ WU Wien Zurück Jetzt bewerben! Office Koordinator*in Wirtschaftsuniversität Wien Büro, Verwaltung, Sachbearbeitung Teilzeit Publizierung bis: 11.11.2026 Sie wollen mit Ihrer Arbeit etwas bewegen, Verantwortung übernehmen und so die Rahmenbedingungen für Spitzenforschung und -lehre schaffen? Bei uns finden Sie das Umfeld, in dem Sie Ihr Potenzial entfalten können. An einer der größten und modernsten Wirtschaftsuniversitäten Europas. Auf einem Campus, an dem Arbeitsqualität auch Lebensqualität ist. Wir suchen Verstärkung am Department-Office Volkswirtschaft Teilzeit, 15 Stunden/Woche Ab 12.01.2027 befristet bis 30.09.2029 Sie organisieren und kommunizieren gerne und möchten die Volkswirtschaft an der WU aus der Nähe kennenlernen? In dieser abwechslungsreichen Rolle sind Sie die zentrale Schnittstelle zwischen akademischer Einheit, Department, Studierenden und Lehrenden und halten mit Überblick und Hands-on-Mentalität den Betrieb am Laufen. Was Sie erwartet Finanzen: Sie verwalten Budgets in SAP, erstellen Finanzberichte, bearbeiten Reisekostenabrechnungen, Refundierungen und die gesamte Rechnungsabwicklung Ihrer akademischen Einheit. Drittmittel-Projekte: Sie unterstützen wissenschaftliche Mitarbeiter*innen bei Einreichung, Verwaltung, Finanzberichten und Abrechnung von Drittmittel-Projekten, behalten den Budget-Überblick in SAP und sorgen für fristgerechte, korrekte Dokumentation. Sekretariat & Infrastruktur: Sie unterstützen Ihre akademische Einheit und das Department Office selbstständig in der Verwaltung, buchen Lehrräume, bereiten Meetings vor, erledigen kleinere Bestellungen und stellen sicher, dass Ausstattung und Technik in Büros, sonst. Räumen und Teeküchen funktionieren; Störungen melden Sie proaktiv an die Serviceeinheiten. Zudem betreuen Sie Mitarbeiter*innen und Gäste, inklusive Hotel- und Restaurantreservierungen. Weiters organisieren gelegentlich kleine Veranstaltungen, etc. Datenbanken & Publikationen: Sie pflegen die Forschungsdatenbank PURE laufend und erfassen Research Papers sowie Publikationen des Departments zuverlässig und vollständig. Front Office: Sie unterstützen 1x/Woche das Front-Office-Team, empfangen Studierende, Lektor*innen, Gäste und Lieferant*innen und arbeiten bei der Department-Verwaltung mit. Web & Kommunikation: Sie halten die Webseiteninhalte Ihrer akademischen Einheit und des Departments aktuell (CMS: TYPO3) und sorgen für klare, zielgruppengerechte Informationen. Lehrveranstaltungsadministration: Sie verwalten die Verträge externer Lehrender und kommunizieren professionell mit Lehrenden und Studierenden und beantworten Fragen rund um Lehrveranstaltungen. Was Sie mitbringen Matura, oder gleichwertige kaufmännische Ausbildung (z.B. kaufm. Kolleg, HAK). IT-Kompetenz: Sehr sicherer Umgang mit Microsoft 365; Kenntnisse in SAP, TYPO3, KI-Tools und Lernplattformen sind von Vorteil. Zahlenaffinität: Sie arbeiten gerne und detailgenau mit Zahlen (z.B. in Microsoft 365, Excel und SAP) und behalten dabei die größeren Zusammenhänge im Blick. Erfahrung: Einschlägige Berufserfahrung als Assistenz oder im Sekretariat und in der Verwaltung von Drittmitteln; Kenntnisse im Bildungsbereich sind wünschenswert. Eine hohe Bereitschaft zum selbstständigen Lernen wird vorausgesetzt. Engagement: Eigeninitiative, Zuverlässigkeit, vorausschauendes Arbeiten und Anpackmentalität. Arbeitsweise: Ausgeprägter Teamspirit, Organisationstalent und Gelassenheit auch in intensiveren Phasen. Sprache und Kommunikation: Hervorragende Deutsch- und sehr gute Englischkenntnisse (mind. C1) in Wort und Schrift; professionelle, serviceorientierte Kommunikation mit unterschiedlichen Zielgruppen. Was wir Ihnen bieten Flexible Arbeitszeiten im Rahmen der Gleitzeit Mobiles Arbeiten Vielfältiges Angebot an Weiterbildung Zahlreiche Benefits , von Betriebsarzt über Sportangebote und Essenszuschuss bis hin zu vielfältigen Mitarbeitenden-Rabatten Sinnstiftende Arbeit , in einem weltoffenen, inklusiven und familienfreundlichen Arbeitsklima Architektonisch herausragender, moderner Campus mitten in Wien Inspirierendes Campusleben mit über 2.400 Mitarbeitenden in Forschung, Lehre und Verwaltung und rund 21.500 Studierenden Sehr gute öffentliche Erreichbarkeit Neugierig geworden? Mehr darüber was die WU als Arbeitgeberin besonders macht, erfahren Sie unter www.wu.ac.at/benefits Das monatliche Mindestentgelt beträgt 1.145,06 Euro brutto. Tätigkeitsbezogene Vordienstzeiten können zu einem höheren Einstiegsgehalt führen. Darüber hinaus bieten wir eine Vielzahl an attraktiven Sozialleistungen an. Wollen Sie Teil der WU werden? Dann bewerben Sie sich bitte bis spätestens 11.11.2026 (Kennzahl: 2938). Wir freuen uns auf Sie! Die WU schätzt Diversität und Inklusion und bemüht sich aktiv um ein vielfältiges Team. Sie sind sich nicht sicher, ob Ihr Profil unseren Anforderungen entspricht? Bewerben Sie sich trotzdem! Frauen werden bei gleicher Qualifikation bevorzugt aufgenommen. Bewerber*innen mit Behinderungen werden in allen Phasen des Bewerbungsprozesses unterstützt. IMPRESSUM DATENSCHUTZ Cookieeinstellungen Close Einstellungen Cookies Notwendige Cookies Diese Cookies sind für die Funktionalität unserer Website erforderlich\nund können in unserem System nicht ausgeschaltet werden. Vorausgewählt Webstatistik Wir verwenden diese Cookies, um statistische Informationen über unsere Website\nbereitzustellen. Sie werden zur Leistungsmessung und -verbesserung verwendet. Wählen Soziale Netzwerke & Embeds Auf einigen Seiten betten wir Inhalte von Sozialen Netzwerken und anderen Diensten ein. Dadurch können Ihre personenbezogenen Daten an den Betreiber des Portals, von dem der Inhalt stammt, weitergegeben werden, so dass dieser Ihr Verhalten analysieren kann. Wählen Notwendige Cookies sid Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 1 Stunde Enthält eine anonyme Nutzer-ID, um mehrere Anfragen eines Nutzers derselben HTTP-Session zuordnen zu können. cookieconsent_status Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Tage Dieses Cookie speichert Ihre Cookie-Einstellungen für diese Website. Webstatistik _pk_id* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 13 Monate Registriert eine eindeutige ID für einen Website-Besucher, die protokolliert, wie der Besucher die Website verwendet. Die Daten werden für Statistiken verwendet. _pk_ref* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at    Ablauf: 6 Monate Dieses Cookie wird als Referenz zur anonymen Tracking-Session auf der Seite eingesetzt. _pk_ses* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Minuten Dieses Cookie speichert eine eindeutige Session-ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: Dieses Session Cookie wird beim Schließen des Browsers wieder gelöscht Dieses Cookie speichert den Website-Besuch auf Basis einer Session- oder Visitor-ID. Anpassung speichern Abbrechen"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Postdoctoral-Researcher-Project-staff-eng-j2945.html": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher (Project staff)",
      "description": "Job opportunity Postdoctoral Researcher (Project staff) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Postdoctoral Researcher (Project staff) Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-18 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Language and Discourse in Business Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting as soon as possible, and ending after 2 years and 9 months Qualified candidates with disabilities are especially encouraged to apply for this position. If necessary, a reduction of the extent of employment is possible. You have a passion for the English language and linguistics, and are interested in studying the ‘dark side’ of business communication? You would like to engage in research that is meaningful and has social impact? The Institute for Language and Discourse in Business is currently inviting applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher (Project Staff). What to expect This position is advertised as part of the FWF-funded ‘Examining discourses of corporate environmental wrongdoing’ project (10.55776/ESP2112125), led by Dr. Mathew Gillings in the Institute for Language and Discourse in Business. The project focuses on the discursive construction of corporate environmental wrongdoing from a range of stakeholder perspectives. It is a full-time, fixed-term, postdoctoral researcher position made up of the following key parts: Research: Working as part of a project team, you will conduct research focusing on the discourses of corporate wrongdoing, crisis communication, and corporate sustainability communication. Research output: You will engage in innovative research and publish it in high-quality outlets, particularly in the area of corpus-assisted discourse studies and corpus pragmatics. Research support: You will collaborate within the team, engage in data collection, and support publishing activities. Research funding: You will offer support in applying for research funding. Organizational tasks: You will support senior faculty in their research, teaching, and administration. Networking: You will have the opportunity to create your own professional network. What you have to offer A doctoral degree: You hold a completed doctoral degree in English language and/or linguistics and/or business communication. Research profile: You have a research orientation that is strongly aligned with that of the Institute for Language and Discourse in Business, as well as an interest in engaging in research projects focusing on the discourse of corporate wrongdoing. Research output: You have a promising portfolio of high-quality publications (commensurate with academic age), demonstrating academic rigour and relevance. Advanced skills: You have strong theoretical and methodological competence, particularly in corpus linguistics, discourse studies and pragmatics, and you have experience in corpus compilation and annotation. You have experience of working with programs and tools allowing for the compilation and analysis of large corpora (e.g., R, Sketch Engine, Python, etc.). Research funding: You have potential for acquiring research funding. International experience: Academic experience in an international, preferably anglophone, environment is a plus. Language skills: Expert command of spoken and written English; a willingness to develop a working knowledge of spoken and written German. Social skills: You are highly motivated, able to work in teams, and communicate effectively with both internal and external stakeholders. Organizational skills: You have experience in website administration and social media communication. What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,014.30 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 18, 2026 (ID 2945). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Project-staff-member-post-doc-eng-j2922.html": {
      "title": "Job opportunity Project staff member (post-doc)",
      "description": "Job opportunity Project staff member (post-doc) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Project staff member (post-doc) Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-28 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Ecological Economics Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting December 01, 2026, and ending after 14 months (potential extension based on performance) Be part of an international research team contributing to shape the future of climate and nature finance within the international financial architecture. Work with top scholars to develop models for policy and financial impact. We are looking for a post-doctoral researcher in climate and nature finance, with a focus and interest on their international development aspects. The position is based at the Institute for Ecological Economics, within the Vienna University of Economics and Business, under the supervision of Irene Monasterolo. You will work with the experts of the Task Force on Climate, Development and the International Financial Architecture led by Boston University in collaboration with the G24 and V20 on reshaping international climate finance for development, in dialogue with multinational development banks and financial institutions. Within the project, you will contribute to inform how different financial arrangements and instruments could contribute to build resilience to climate and nature risks, in an inclusive and financial stability-aware way. You will explore the conditions for climate development finance to act a global shock absorber in the context of climate and nature risks. In particular, you will provide new conceptual and quantitative insights on debt, financial instruments and measures (e.g. Resilience and Sustainability Facility, Recovery and Resilience Facility, Capital Flow Management Measures, Regional Financing Arrangements, equity), including a global insurance scheme, for emerging markets and low-income economies (EMDEs). This is a crucial topic for the future of international development: growing socio-economic losses from climate change and ecosystem depletion, and geopolitical instability, contribute to decrease countries’ fiscal space and to increase the cost of investing in resilience. In this context, EMDEs face a future of sluggish development, insufficient resilience and sustainability, and new debt crises, with cascading effects on the economy of Global North countries. You will work in close contact with a team of experts in climate finance for development with long experience in development finance institutions. You will have the opportunity to attend international research and policy workshops, conferences, and have policy impact, shaping the discussion about the international climate finance agenda. What to expect Developing quantitative tools (in particular Stock-Flow Consistent behavioral model and stress test models) for macro-financial risk assessment of climate and nature risks, and financial instruments. Collaborating with top scholars from leading institutions and think tanks (e.g., Boston University, Utrecht University, University of Venice, Bruegel) and engaging with the Task Force team. Driving impact by informing the design of financial instruments and financial policy in EMDEs. Contributing to academic output through publishing high-quality research in peer reviewed high ranked journals. Support the project dissemination activities by participating in relevant conferences, workshops, and seminars. What you have to offer We are looking for a motivated post-doctoral researcher with the following qualifications: PhD in Economics, Finance, Statistics, Physics, or a related field. Proven experience with macro-financial and financial risk modeling, using either Stock-Flow Consistent models, or Agent-Based models, or network models. Expertise and interest with climate and nature finance, and development finance. Strong coding skills in Matlab and Python. Fluency in English both spoken and written (other languages are a plus) and willingness to travel international for conferences and meetings. Ability to deliver quality and relevant work, meet deadlines, manage tasks independently, work in team. Ability to write and present research for academic and policy audiences independently. Location: Vienna, one of the cities with the highest quality of life in Europe, with access to facilities and a dynamic international research environment. Remuneration: in accordance with the applicable collective labour agreement, including social security coverage and paid annual leave. To apply, please send your curriculum vitae, including a letter of motivation and at least two published or unpublished papers. A first round of online interviews will take place at the beginning of November. Expected starting date of the position is December 2026. For more information about this position, please contact Prof. Dr. Irene Monasterolo ( irene.monasterolo@wu.ac.at ). What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €3,760.73 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2922). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"
