    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Project-staff-member-pre-doc-eng-j2928.html": {
      "title": "Job opportunity Project staff member (pre-doc)",
      "description": "Job opportunity Project staff member (pre-doc) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Project staff member (pre-doc) Vienna University of Economics and Business IT Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-11-11 Do you want to use data to understand why the energy transition is so hard, and how to accelerate it? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential, at one of Europe's largest and most modern business and economics universities, on a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Data, Energy, and Sustainability Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting January 01, 2027, and limited until September 30, 2029 We are hiring a pre-doctoral researcher (project staff, 30 hours/week) at the Institute for Data, Energy, and Sustainability (IDEaS), led by Prof. Kavita Surana and supported by the BMIMI Endowed Professorship for Data-Driven Knowledge Generation: Climate Action. The position starts on January 1, 2027 and ends on September 30, 2029. What to expect You will join a research group that develops data-driven evidence for energy transitions and climate action, starting from the research question and then building the data needed to answer it. This position focuses on (i) why capital-intensive energy technologies and infrastructures, such as offshore wind, geothermal, hydrogen, carbon capture, utilization and storage (CCUS), and energy grids, succeed or stall, and (ii) how technology, firms, investors, and policy shape those outcomes. You will build novel datasets by designing pipelines that combine and harmonize sources, with a special emphasis on turning unstructured and scattered information into structured, validated data using NLP, large language models (LLMs), or other relevant methods. You will then analyze these data with empirical methods, such as econometrics and statistical or network analysis. You will work in a highly interdisciplinary, international environment, with dedicated mentoring and regular, constructive feedback to support your growth as a researcher. As part of the institute's team, your responsibilities will include: Conducting research: You will contribute to the institute's research projects, build and maintain high-quality datasets and data pipelines, and publish in leading international peer-reviewed journals. Writing a dissertation: You will pursue a PhD at WU and devote one third of your working hours to your dissertation, which can complement your project work Supervision: You will co-supervise bachelor's and/or master's theses. Engaging with external stakeholders: You will work with the institute's partners in industry, government, and academia to co-develop and communicate research insights. Supporting organizational duties: You will take on organizational and administrative tasks for the institute. Supporting teaching: Independent teaching within this position is available to support your career path -- non-continuous teaching of max. 3 SWS is supported as part of an external teaching assignment outside working hours. Within working hours, you will support the institute's teaching, including preparing course materials and assisting with the organization and delivery of courses at the bachelor's and/or master's level. What you have to offer Academic degree: You have a master's degree (or equivalent) that qualifies you for enrollment in a doctoral program at WU, in a quantitative or analytical field such as data science, computer science, information systems, statistics, mathematics, physics, economics, or engineering (especially with a focus on empirical or data analysis). An interdisciplinary degree in the social sciences, public policy, or management with substantial quantitative training also qualifies. Essential skills: Building datasets: Demonstrated experience constructing datasets from unstructured or heterogeneous sources, and motivation to build novel datasets rather than only analyze existing ones. Coding: Advanced proficiency in Python or R, including version control, shown through projects, a thesis, or code you can share. Empirical analysis: Training in econometrics or statistics. Interest in energy and climate: Genuine motivation to work on the energy transition, especially on capital-intensive energy technologies and infrastructure. Experience in any of the following is a plus: web scraping and data collection, document and information extraction, data integration and entity resolution, NLP and large language models, knowledge graphs, network science or complex systems, and a background in energy technology innovation, climate tech, energy policy, climate finance, industrial policy, or energy economics. You do not need all of these. We care more about how you approach a data problem than about any specific method. Language skills: You have excellent skills of written and spoken English. Knowledge of German (or willingness to learn it) is a plus. Working style: You take ownership of your work and enjoy being part of a team where people contribute to each other's success. You set high standards for yourself, care as much about asking the right question as about applying the right method, and thrive in an interdisciplinary, collaborative environment where you engage with multiple audiences. Please submit at least the following documents with your application: (a) A motivation letter (max. 2 pages) in which you engage critically with a recent paper (published in the last 3 years) by scholars in our group on the scaling or development of energy technologies or infrastructure. For example, you might discuss a limitation in its data or approach, a question it leaves open, or a dataset that could extend it. Explain the research directions you would like to pursue building on this paper, including the question that interests you and the data sources you would need to develop. (b) A curriculum vitae, including a list of publications (if applicable) and the names and contact details of two references (prior employers or academic supervisors). (c) Transcripts and grades from your master's and bachelor's studies, including your master's or diploma thesis grade. (d) A work sample that demonstrates your data science skills, e.g., a link to a code repository (GitHub or similar), your master's thesis, or a paper. We particularly encourage women to apply, including those from analytical fields who are new to energy or climate topics but have a strong interest in them. Please direct any questions to Prof. Kavita Surana at kavita.surana@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €2,877.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2928). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2942.html": {
      "title": "Research and Teaching Associate",
      "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-11-18 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Department for Business Communication Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting January 01, 2027, and ending after 6 years Would you like to understand connections and make a difference? Are you interested in communication and science? We offer you an environment where you can develop your potential. At one of the largest and most modern business universities in Europe. On a campus where quality of work equals quality of life. We are looking for new members to join the team at the Department of Business Communication at Vienna University of Economics and Business. Our societies are facing enormous challenges—artificial intelligence, global warming, and increasing global system competition are just a few of the contextual factors that influence organizations of all types, sizes, and forms today. At the same time, these organizations play a crucial role in overcoming these challenges and implementing and supporting transformation processes. Strategic communication is essential here for sense making, building and maintaining stakeholder relationships, but also for dealing with the consequences of a highly polarized information and media society. This position opens the door to an academic career in research and teaching in the field of strategic communication with a focus on quantitative empirical research. Are you interested? Do you already have an idea for a dissertation, a burning question you want to solve? Then apply and become a member of our creative, international, and inspiring team at the Department of Business Communication at WU Vienna. What to expect As a member of our team, you will actively participate in research, teaching, and administration. This includes Writing your dissertation: You will conduct research on your topic and spend one-third of your working time on your dissertation. Research: Participating in research projects. Engaging in international publication and presentation activities. Contributing to project applications and third-party funding acquisition. Independent teaching (2 hours of teaching per week / semester / after the first year). Student support: Co-Supervision and supporting students. Administration: Participating in evaluation measures and administrative tasks at the Department of Business Communication. What you have to offer Degree: You have completed your master's degree in business communication, communication studies, or a related degree to qualify you for doctoral studies at WU. Subject-specific competences desirable in the fields of (strategic, organizational, business or political) communication or corporate communications. Language skills: fluent command of English at C1 level, and willingness to learn German (if not already a proficient German speaker). Methodological knowledge: sound knowledge of data analysis and quantitative methods, particularly survey designs and experimental research, is expected. Publications and outreach: ideally first experiences in academic publishing. IT-Skills: Sound knowledge of R or Python is expected. First Teaching experience in higher education is desirable; you are also prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats and innovative approaches, and to develop and hone your teaching skills; you are willing to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €2,877.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 18, 2026 (ID 2942). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2944.html": {
      "title": "Research and Teaching Associate",
      "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-11-11 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Ecological Economics Part-time, 15 hours/week Starting November 16, 2026, and limited until December 31, 2027 Few researchers get the chance to build an institution from the ground up. Do you want to help found WU's new home for energy research, and connect it to one of the world's densest energy ecosystems right here in Vienna? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential, at one of Europe's largest and most modern business and economics universities, on a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are hiring a predoc researcher (15 hours/week) to contribute to the new research cluster Energy Transitions and Future Energy Systems that unites energy researchers across WU's departments. The position covers the cluster's founding period, from November 16, 2026 to December 31, 2027. What to expect Your tasks include contributing to the cluster’s build-up, which is led by its founding Senior Scientist, and benefit from a structure that is being set up to serve exactly the kind of work you will be doing. You are also expected to undertake your own research. You will work on a doctoral thesis on a topic within the cluster’s thematic scope, supervised by one of the coordinating professors and embedded in a community of researchers across departments. This is a launch year: you will see an academic institution being built from the inside and help shape it, while keeping clear time and space for your doctoral work. Your responsibilities will include: Contributing to the cluster’s research activities: You will support the Senior Scientist and the coordinating professors on the substantive side of the build-up, for instance by contributing to the research workshops and the speaker series, helping prepare collaborative grant applications, and producing background analyses for the cluster’s engagement with policymakers, businesses, and international organizations. The cluster’s day-to-day operations are handled by the Senior Scientist and a team of student assistants, so your contribution is as a researcher, not as an administrator. Your own research: You will pursue a doctoral thesis on energy transitions, future energy systems, present your work at international conferences, and publish in peer-reviewed journals, with the support of your supervisor and the cluster’s faculty. Contributing to the shared agenda: You will take part in the cluster’s research workshops, bring your perspective to the development of its problem-focused research agenda, and co-author papers with cluster faculty where this fits your thesis. Connecting early-career researchers: You will help build and animate a network of predoctoral researchers working on energy across WU, together with the Senior Scientist who mentors this group. Teaching: You will contribute to teaching at the institute in line with the standard workload for this position (1 hour per semester). What you have to offer A completed master’s degree in economics, socio-economics or ecological economics, or a related field, completed by the starting date at the latest A strong interest in energy transitions and a research idea, or an openness to developing one, within the cluster’s thematic scope Solid methodological training, quantitative or qualitative, appropriate to your intended research; experience with energy systems modelling and participatory methods and processes is an advantage Curiosity about interdisciplinary work and the ability to engage with colleagues from economics, law, management, and technology Excellent written and spoken English; German is an advantage but not required Initiative, reliability, and the ability to organize your own work within a collaborative setting Please submit at least the following documents with your application: Please submit your application, including a cover letter, CV, academic transcripts, a short research statement (max. 2 pages) outlining a possible thesis topic within the cluster’s scope. Please direct any questions to: stagl@wu.ac.at What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €1,416.04 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2944). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2948.html": {
      "title": "Research and Teaching Associate",
      "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-11-18 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Cognition & Behavior Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting as soon as possible, and ending after 6 years The position is part of the Institute for Cognition and Behavior headed by Prof. Susann Fiedler. We investigate how attention, motivation and social contexts shape judgment and behavior. Current research includes belief formation and updating, motivated cognition and willful ignorance, cooperation and ethical decision, and effects of AI on human judgment, learning and scientific work. We combine laboratory and online experiments with process tracing. What to expect Enroll in the PhD program and conduct your dissertation research at the institute (an active participant pool, an experimental group lab as well as eye-tracking lab will be available). You will be investigating your research topic and spending a third of your working hours on writing your dissertation. Plan and run laboratory and online studies, analyze behavioral data, and maintain reproducible research materials, data documentation and analysis code Teaching (e.g., within the specialization (SBWL) “Decision Sciences: Game Theory, Psychology and Data Analysis”) Attendance of international conferences Publication of research projects in international journals What you have to offer Master’s degree in psychology, cognitive science, economics, business and management (alternatively in a related field) that qualifies you for enrollment in a doctoral program at WU Interested in one of the following fields: decision making, information processing, cooperation, trust, bounded ethicality, process tracing Strong background and interest in empirical social science methodology / statistics Ability to formulate testable research questions, justify methodological choices, and critically evaluate alternative explanations and limitations. Experience with online experiment implementation, computational modelling, LLMs, eye-tracking or mouse-tracking are welcome. These specialist skills are not required on entry. Fluency in English and the ability to explain research ideas clearly in writing and discussion. Ability to organize research tasks reliably, collaborate across disciplines, and give and use constructive feedback. You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats Application materials: Additional to a conventional motivation letter, please submit short answers to the following two questions (maximum 450 words in total; bullet points are welcome): 1. Describe one methodological decision you made or helped make in a research project, thesis, or coursework assignment. What was your own contribution? Which alternative did you consider, why did you choose your approach, and what limitation remained? 2. Identify a research question within one of the institute’s research areas that you would like to investigate. State a testable hypothesis, briefly outline an experiment, and explain what result would make you reconsider your hypothesis. We value concrete examples and reflection on limitations. A fully developed research proposal is not expected. Shortlisted applicants will be invited to interviews during the first two weeks of December. Language-editing tools may be used when preparing the application; if generative AI contributed to the substantive content, briefly state how and what you checked; this statement does not count towards the word limit. What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €2.832,08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 18, 2026 (ID 2948). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Senior-Scientist-post-doc-eng-j2939.html": {
      "title": "Senior Scientist, post-doc",
      "description": "Job opportunity Senior Scientist, post-doc at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Senior Scientist, post-doc Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-11-11 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Data, Energy, and Sustainability Part-time, 20 hours/week Starting January 01, 2027, and limited until December 31, 2027 Few researchers get the chance to build an institution from the ground up. Do you want to found WU's new home for energy research, and connect it to one of the world's densest energy ecosystems right here in Vienna? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential, at one of Europe's largest and most modern business and economics universities, on a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. What to expect You will help build a home for energy research at WU. Energy Transitions and Future Energy Systems is a new research cluster that brings together leading scholars from multiple departments, spanning economics, finance, law, policy, management, and technology, and initiated and coordinated by Professors Jürgen Braunstein, Sigrid Stagl, and Kavita Surana. It tackles the questions that will define the energy transition at the local, national, European, and international level, for instance: how to keep energy affordable while decarbonizing industry, how to secure supply chains and strategic autonomy, how to steer capital toward climate-aligned investment, how to overcome grid and permitting bottlenecks, and how the rapid growth of AI and data centers will reshape energy systems. Our ambition is to build a leading academic think tank on energy: one that connects rigorous research in economics, business, law, and policy with the decisions of governments, companies, and international organizations. You will be the first person dedicated to building it. As the cluster's founding Senior Scientist, you will turn a group of strong individual researchers into a community with a shared agenda and connect it to one of the world's densest energy ecosystems. Vienna is home to Austria's energy regulator and ministries, major utilities, and multiple international organizations, all within reach of WU's campus. This is a launch year: the role is designed for an established researcher with their own funded research program who wants to take on an institution-building role, and to lay the foundations that will carry the cluster forward. You will work closely with the cluster's faculty and have latitude to shape its future. Your responsibilities will include: Shaping the agenda: You will lead a series of research workshops with faculty across departments to define a shared, problem-focused research agenda and identify where collaboration adds the most value. Building for the long term: You will develop the cluster's funding and governance model and lead collaborative, multi-PI grant applications for third-party, institutional, and partner funding that anchor its long-term research program. Running the cluster: You will manage the cluster's day-to-day operations with the support of a small team of student assistants, from organizing meetings and events to budgets, reporting, communications, and its web presence. Much of this role is hands-on, and getting these foundations right is what will allow the cluster to last. Convening the community: You will bring WU's energy researchers together through workshops and a speaker series, and lay the groundwork for a future flagship energy forum. Opening doors: You will initiate partnerships with policymakers, businesses, external scholars, and international organizations, and begin bringing WU research into energy debates in Vienna, Austria, Europe, and beyond. Supporting early-career researchers: You will mentor predoctoral researchers working on energy across WU and help build a visible network for them. Continuing and advancing your own research: You will lead or support co-authored papers from this cluster and benefit from new collaborations across the cluster. What you have to offer Academic degree: You hold a PhD in economics, social sciences, management, public policy, law, energy systems, engineering, or any related field, and have established yourself as a researcher on energy related questions. Essential skills: o Research standing: A strong publication record in leading peer-reviewed journals and an active research program that you will continue alongside this role, ideally with funding secured beyond the first year of this position. o Bringing people together: A track record of building collaborations across disciplines, for example through joint projects, research networks, or workshops you have led. o S ecuring funding: Experience preparing competitive grant applications, ideally collaborative or multi-PI proposals. o Interest in building an institution: Motivation to shape a new research community and make WU a reference point in energy research and debate. Experience in any of the following is a plus: work at a research center, think tank, international organization, regulator, or company at the interface of research and policy; policy-facing outputs such as briefs or consultation responses; networks in the Austrian or European energy community; and familiarity with EU energy and industrial policy. You do not need all of these. We care more about how you would bring people and ideas together than about any individual credential. Language skills: You have excellent written and spoken English. Knowledge of German (or willingness to learn it) is a plus. Working style: You enjoy making others successful and building something larger than your own work. You are comfortable working across disciplines and with academic, policy, and business audiences, and can move an agenda forward without formal authority. You bring strategic vision and are just as comfortable with the operational detail of running an initiative day to day. Please submit at least the following documents with your application: (a) A vision statement (max. 2 pages) in which you choose one challenge facing the energy transition, within or across the cluster's themes, and outline how you would bring WU's researchers together around it in the first year: the question, the disciplines and partners involved, and a funding route that could sustain the work. (b) A curriculum vitae, including a list of publications, current and past research funding, and the names and contact details of two references. (c) A short description (max. 1 page) of a collaboration, network, or event you initiated or led, and what came out of it. Please direct any questions to: juergen.braunstein@wu.ac.at What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €2,539.75 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2939). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2953.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-25 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Department of Economics Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting September 01, 2027, and ending after 6 years Qualified candidates with disabilities are especially encouraged to apply for this position. If necessary, a reduction of the extent of employment is possible. The Department of Economics of the WU Vienna University of Economics and Business invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant Professor position (post-doc) in Industrial Economics. The position is a 100% (40 hours/week, employee subject to the terms of the Collective Bargaining Agreement for University Staff - Angestellte*r gemäß Kollektivvertrag für die Arbeitnehmer*innen der Universitäten). The position will be limited to a period of six years and is expected to begin on September 1, 2027. What to expect The Department of Economics offers an active and internationally oriented research environment. The successful candidates’ research focus should be in the field of Industrial Economics. You will join the faculty of the Department of Economics and are expected to provide a good fit to its current research environment, as well as to cultivate excellence and contribute to the research, teaching, and service activities in the department. What you have to offer Applicants should have a solid academic qualification (PhD or equivalent) in Economics (or a related field), high-quality research output (job market paper(s) and/or publications in international peer-reviewed journals) related to the field of industrial economics, a commitment to excellence in teaching including the willingness to use multimedia teaching methods, experience in the acquisition of third-party funded projects is of advantage, and ability to enlarge and deepen the network of contacts to the international academic community. Following supporting documents need to be submitted with your application: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Up to two research papers Three reference letters Teaching evaluations First-round interviews will be conducted virtually at the EJM, Dec 14-17, 2026. Applicants should also apply through the EJM platform. To be considered for the first round of interviews, all application materials must be received by November 25, 2026. What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,079.50 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 25, 2026 (ID 2953). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
    },
    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-tenure-track-qualification-agreement-eng-j2954.html": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, tenure track (qualification agreement)",
      "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, tenure track (qualification agreement) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, tenure track (qualification agreement) Vienna University of Economics and Business Commercial professions (other) Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-25 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Department of Economics Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting September 01, 2027, and limited for 6 years Qualified candidates with disabilities are especially encouraged to apply for this position. If necessary, a reduction of the extent of employment is possible. A qualification agreement will be concluded at the start of the employment (§ 27 of the Collective Bargaining Agreement). Pursuant to WU’s Personnel Development Plan, this position can only be fixed-term for up to six years. Once all objectives agreed upon in the qualification agreement have been fulfilled, the employment relationship can be made permanent. Employees who have successfully completed a qualification agreement are classified as associate professors. From an organizational regulation perspective they belong to the group of professors. Three years after successful completion of the qualification agreement, they are entitled to apply for promotion to full professor according to the By-Laws of WU § 43a. The Department of Economics invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor position (post-doc) in International Economics. What to expect The Department of Economics offers an active and internationally oriented research environment. The successful candidates’ research focus should be in the field of International Economics. You will join the faculty of the Department of Economics and are expected to provide a good fit to its current research environment, as well as to cultivate excellence and contribute to the research, teaching, and service activities in the department. What you have to offer Applicants should have a solid academic qualification (PhD or equivalent) in economics (or a related field), high-quality research output (job market paper(s) and/or publications in international peer-reviewed journals) related to the field of international economics, academic mobility, proven by either having completed their PhD or doctoral degree at a university other than WU, or having completed an uninterrupted postdoc employment period (in a tenure-track or non-tenure-track position) of at least two years and with an extent of employment of at least 20 hours per week at another university or non-academic research institution, a commitment to excellence in teaching including the willingness to use multimedia teaching methods, experience in the acquisition of third-party funded projects is of advantage, and ability to enlarge and deepen the network of contacts to the international academic community. Following supporting documents need to be submitted with your application: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Up to two research papers Three reference letters Teaching evaluations Research Statement Teaching Statement First-round interviews will be conducted virtually at the EJM Conference Dec 14-17, 2026. Applicants should also apply through the EJM platform. To be considered for first-round interviews, all application materials must be received by November 25, 2026. What we offer you Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,980.80 (14 times per year). In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 25, 2026 (ID 2954). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"
